CE FND-132 gate: the ONLY corpus deck that reaches the conductor-path basis.
CE Two wires meeting START-to-START at (0,0,3) and running outward and down.
CE What routes a deck here is needing a traversal REVERSAL to walk the two wires
CE as one conductor. Measured 2026-08-30, of the four ways two wires can meet:
CE   start-to-start          paths
CE   end-to-end              paths
CE   start of 1 meets end of 2   paths
CE   end of 1 meets start of 2   PLAIN basis (already a chain in deck order)
CE So the one case that does NOT route is the one people write by hand without
CE thinking about it -- wires listed in the order you would walk them.
CE Probed 2026-08-30: of every deck then in corpus/, ZERO routed here, so
CE PH9-CHK-002 was reachable only from in-source unit tests -- and FND-121, a
CE CRITICAL finding about this very basis being wired to one frontend of four,
CE was found by audit rather than by the corpus, because the corpus could not
CE reach the code at all.
CE fnec 264.882179 + j410.856326; nec2c 268.56 + j452.26 on the same deck
CE (R within 1.4%, X within 9.2%) -- inside the documented Hallen-vs-nec2c
CE systematic, and the same pair of numbers FND-121 recorded when the four
CE frontends disagreed by 29x.
